        "original_id": "a1621cdb-7f8a-5bb3-a405-d37157ddc2d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: Comic Court\n- Events: Melbourne Cup\n- Places: Australia, Australasia\n- Concepts: Thoroughbred horse racing, race records\n\nFacts:\n- Comic Court was a post-war Australian-bred Thoroughbred racehorse active from 1945 to 1973.\n- Comic Court was noted for versatility and set race records at 6 furlongs (1,200 metres) and 2 miles (3,200 metres).\n- In 1950, Comic Court won the Melbourne Cup while carrying 9 st.\n- In 1950, Comic Court set an Australasian record of 3 minutes 19½ seconds in the Melbourne Cup.\n- The Melbourne Cup is Australia's most prestigious annual Thoroughbred horse race.",
